SUMMARY:MCP Live!
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nThe Model Context Protocol (MCP) is
  the open standard for connecting AI models to tools and data.\n\nThis hal
 f-day event covers MCP end to end: its role as an open standard\, how it's
  adopted across the developer ecosystem\, and hands-on sessions on buildin
 g MCP servers.\n\nIt also addresses enterprise readiness including authent
 ication\, governance\, and security.\n\n[Get started with Model Context Pr
 otocol](https://aka.ms/MCP/getstarted/reactor)\n\n**Agenda:**\n\n| Session
  Title | Speaker(s) | Speaker Company |\n|--------------------------------
 --------|----------------------------|---------------------|\n| Welcome to
  MCP Live! | Liam Hampton\, Pamela Fox | Microsoft\, Microsoft |\n| State 
 of MCP | Caitie McCaffrey | Microsoft |\n| MCP: Server\, Client & Protocol
  at GitHub | Sam Morrow | Microsoft |\n| A unified MCP layer with Toolboxe
 s in Microsoft Foundry | Viswajeeet Balaji | Microsoft |\n| Building MCP s
 ervers with VS Code | Harald Kirschner | Microsoft |\n| MCP Authorization:
  DCR\, EMA\, and More! | Sam Bellen\, Den Delimarsky | Okta/Auth0\, Anthro
 pic |\n| When chatbots grow buttons: Building MCP apps with FastMCP | Jere
 miah Lowin | Prefect |\n| Event-driven agents\, powered by MCP | Clare Lig
 uori | AWS |\n| Closing | Liam Hampton\, Pamela Fox | Microsoft\, Microsof
 t
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3156
 19188/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260709T201629Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260709T201629Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_316020803@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T042012Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T140000
SUMMARY:The Quote-to-Cash Blind Spot: Secret Scanning for Enterprise Reven
 ue Systems
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nEvery CPQ\, CLM\, and billing rollo
 ut I've run wires Salesforce or Vlocity to DocuSign\, Stripe or Zuora-type
  billing\, and ERP through API keys and OAuth tokens sitting in DataRaptor
 s\, Integration Procedures\, and deployment scripts. AppSec teams usually 
 classify that layer as "business configuration\," so it never gets scanned
  the way application code does.\n\nWhere credentials actually live in a qu
 ote-to-cash stack: middleware scripts\, integration procedures\, CI/CD for
  CPQ deployments. Why "business systems" teams don't think of themselves a
 s a scanning target\, and what that costs. How GitHub Advanced Security's 
 secret scanning\, push protection\, and custom patterns close the gap\, ev
 en for teams that don't see themselves as developers.\n\nA sample repo mod
 eling a CPQ integration script with a hardcoded OAuth token and API key. P
 ush protection blocking a commit in real time. A custom regex pattern buil
 t for an enterprise revenue-tool token format. The alert triage view a sec
 urity lead would actually work from.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3160
 20803/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260807T171643Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260807T171643Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_316018704@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T042012Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T130000
SUMMARY:Working With Your Data\, Safely: Files\, Approvals and Memory
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nSo far the agent can talk about mar
 kets but cannot touch anything of yours\, and nothing stops it doing somet
 hing it should not. This episode fixes both. We give it file access so it 
 reads a real portfolio.csv and writes its reports back to disk\, then put 
 a place_trade tool behind an explicit human approval.\n\nApproving every s
 ingle read gets old fast\, so we add auto-approval rules for the safe call
 s and one custom rule that clears small trades on its own. We finish with 
 durable memory in two forms\, the files the agent curates itself and the f
 acts Foundry extracts automatically\, and watch both survive a restart.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3160
 18704/
